 "notes": [
  "Instances may be [x,y] or {pos:[x,y], assets:{part_id: asset}, texts:{part_id: sample}}.",
  "Job rows in the reference sit at y 517, 683, 850, 1017, 1187, 1356 (generated art drifts 166-170 px); the game uses pitch 168. Wave 3 (collect_events.png) puts the quests panel and the week's chest bar above them, so the list starts at 712 and the first row at 720, where that painting's first row stands once drawn down to the column.",
  "Every job has its own painting, collect/job_<id>: the painting part fills the row's frame window (x 13..173, y 10..146 of the row) with two units to spare on every side, and the tile part lays collect/job_frame -- the grapes row's frame with its window cut out -- over it, so all fifteen rows wear one frame and no painting's edge ever shows.",
  "The quests panel, its tiles, the chest bar and the Golden Hour's wheel are collect_events.png's (art/slices/collect_events.json): everything from that painting's column is drawn down 0.98577 to stand on collect.png's edges (x 166..928); positions here are the painting's, mapped x' = 166 + (x - 156) * 0.98577, y' = 286 + (y - 505) * 0.98577.",
  "The job_row frame keeps row one's grapes tile and the COLLECT button baked; both are always covered by the painting, tile (frame) and button parts drawn over them.",
  "The quests panel keeps its three tiles and their plates baked; the quest_card instances lay each task's mark and words over them.",
  "An instance may carry rects:{part_id:[x,y,w,h]} when its asset has a different native size (icons are drawn at native size, never scaled)."
 ],
